Status: compiled and tested with the dev LLVM build (filc-llvm shell,
build-filnix at this commit) against the pinned Fil-C runtime. It
applies to mbrock/fil-c d6cbb697f74 (branch filnix) and is also pushed
as mbrock/fil-c branch orb/toolchain-asm (69a5692e9a4). Fetch that
branch, or `sed -n '/^From /,$p' this.patch | git am` in a fil-c
checkout.

Verified with the dev clang:
- annotateglobal (-O2) and annotateglobalO0 print "annotate ok 42";
  annotateglobalfail stops with "filc safety error" (ptr >= upper).
  Run by hand (compile, run, check output), not through run-tests.
- Rubber Band's src/RubberBandLiveShifter.cpp compiles; the pinned
  compiler asserts on it.
- An Abseil-style [[clang::annotate]] constructor works at -O0 and -O2.
- commonsym still passes.

Reproducers with the pinned compiler (Fil-C 0.685, d6cbb69):

    __attribute__((annotate("realtime"))) void f(void) {}
    /* clang -c: Assertion `G.getLinkage() != GlobalValue::AppendingLinkage
       || ...` failed in lockDownLinkage */

    int main(void) { int x __attribute__((annotate("a"))) = 1; return x - 1; }
    /* compiles; running it stops with "Unhandled intrinsic:
       llvm.var.annotation" (llvm.ptr.annotation for annotated fields,
       llvm.annotation for __builtin_annotation) */

From 69a5692e9a4c5ca637bdd66b05e2dd7de2f3f5b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Brockman <mikael@brockman.se>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:17:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FilPizlonator: accept __attribute__((annotate)) and
 __builtin_annotation

__attribute__((annotate)) on a function or global makes Clang emit
llvm.global.annotations, an appending global in the llvm.metadata
section, and lockDownLinkage asserted that the only appending globals
are the ctor, dtor and used lists:

    __attribute__((annotate("realtime"))) void f(void) {}

Only tools read the annotations; codegen never emits llvm.metadata.
Erase the global at the start of the pass, together with the
llvm.metadata strings it referenced once nothing else uses them.

Annotations on locals and fields, and __builtin_annotation, compiled
but stopped the program with "Unhandled intrinsic" for
llvm.var.annotation, llvm.ptr.annotation and llvm.annotation. Remove
them with the other irrelevant intrinsics, as codegen does: the first
is dropped and the other two return their first operand.

Tests: annotateglobal, annotateglobalO0, annotateglobalfail.

Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0ed6a-05c1-75a8-bead-f72fc3f40e56
Co-authored-by: Mikael Brockman <mikael@brockman.se>
